meta {
  name: Report your position to a circle
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/circles/:id/positions
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{id}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "latitude": 0.0,
    "longitude": 0.0,
    "accuracyMeters": 0.0,
    "timestampMs": 0
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  Low cadence, over plain REST — circles update on the order of minutes, which does not justify holding a stream open all day. Overwrites in place: no history, no trail. A paused member's report is accepted and discarded rather than refused, so pausing needs no special handling on the device.

  Responses:
  - 204: No Content
  - 400: Not a member, or an unusable position.
}
